// Finding a name. A linear scan over a few dozen entries, done a handful of times
// a frame; a hash would be more code than the whole module saves.
//
// The FIRST match wins, so an item that appears twice in a layout is found at its
// first occurrence. That is the useful answer for a name used as an identifier
// and the harmless one for a name used as a component.

ui_rfind(string name) {
  int p = 0 - 1;
  int i = 0;
  while (i < len((import ui_rn))) {
    p = lst_pick(p, i, (import ui_rn)[i] = name);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return int p;
